WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.107
White light looks simple. It isn't.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.622
Send it through glass, and it comes apart:
every colour it was carrying, side by side.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.246
Red bends the least. Violet bends the most.

4
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.314
Water does it too.

5
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.336
A surface moves, and light gathers into
bright, living lines.

6
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.587
One drop, and the pattern breaks, rings out,
and knits itself back together.

7
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.474
Glass can gather light, as well as split it.

8
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.686
A sphere becomes a lens, and the light it
gathers burns to a single point.

9
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.970
Even now, the lens in your eye is bending
light, to show you this.
